Here is a concise report based on `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue`.

---

### 1. Teacher grid column sizing (`gridTemplateStyle` / `gridTemplateColumns`)

`gridTemplateStyle` is a computed object that only sets **`gridTemplateColumns`**:

```1650:1656:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const gridTemplateStyle = computed(() => {
  const count = visibleTeachers.value.length;
  return {
    // Desktop: prioritize fitting all teacher columns without horizontal scroll.
    gridTemplateColumns: `56px repeat(${Math.max(1, count)}, minmax(0, 1fr))`,
  };
});
```

- First track: **fixed `56px`** (time column).
- Remaining tracks: **`repeat(N, minmax(0, 1fr))`** so all teacher columns **split the leftover width equally** and are allowed to shrink (`minmax(0, …)`).

The comment matches the desktop CSS: the grid is meant to **fit without horizontal scroll** by squeezing columns (not by min-width per teacher on desktop).

---

### 2. `isTeacherGridCompact` — what it is and when it runs

```1657:1657:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const isTeacherGridCompact = computed(() => visibleTeachers.value.length >= 10);
```

It is **`true` when there are 10 or more `visibleTeachers`**. It toggles the **`teacher-grid-compact`** class on the grid (see template line 163).

---

### 3. Teacher column header (`teacher-col`, `teacher-col-header`)

Template (structure):

```168:175:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
            <div v-for="teacher in visibleTeachers" :key="teacher.id" class="teacher-col">
              <div class="teacher-col-header" :style="{ borderTopColor: getTeacherColor(teacher.id) }">
                <div class="teacher-col-avatar" :style="{ background: getTeacherColor(teacher.id) }">{{ teacher.username.charAt(0) }}</div>
                <div class="teacher-col-info">
                  <div class="teacher-col-name">{{ teacher.username }}</div>
                  <div v-if="teacher.roomLabel" class="teacher-col-room">{{ teacher.roomLabel }}</div>
                </div>
              </div>
```

- **Sticky** header (`position: sticky; top: 0`), **64px** tall by default, flex row with **8px gap**, **3px** colored top border from `getTeacherColor`, avatar = first character of `username`, name + optional `roomLabel` (“教室 …”).

---

### 4. CSS variables for teacher column width

There is **no** dedicated CSS variable for teacher column width. Width comes from the **inline `gridTemplateColumns`** string above. Related tokens are things like `var(--border-color)`, `var(--bg-muted)` for borders/backgrounds, not column width.

---

### 5. Horizontal scrolling / overflow

Default / desktop-oriented rules **hide** horizontal overflow:

```3512:3524:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.week-view {
  ...
  overflow: hidden;
  overflow-x: hidden;
}
.teacher-grid-wrapper {
  overflow-x: hidden;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}
```

On **narrow viewports** (`max-width: 768px`), horizontal scroll is enabled for the week view + grid wrapper, and the grid gets a content-based minimum width:

```4217:4220:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
  .teacher-col { min-width: 0; }
  .week-view { overflow-x: auto; }
  .teacher-grid-wrapper { overflow-x: auto; }
  .teacher-grid { min-width: max-content; }
```

So: **many teachers on desktop = squeeze, not scroll**; **horizontal scroll is mainly a mobile/small-screen behavior.**

---

### 6. `SLOT_HEIGHT` and related sizing

```1432:1437:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const SLOT_HEIGHT = 56;
const SLOT_BORDER = 1;
const SLOT_TOTAL = SLOT_HEIGHT + SLOT_BORDER;
const getBlockHeight = (course) => {
  const dh = course.duration_hours || 1;
  return dh * SLOT_TOTAL - SLOT_BORDER - 6;
};
```

`.slot` and `.time-label` in CSS also use **56px** height (aligned with `SLOT_HEIGHT`).

---

### 7. Teacher filter UI — can teachers be filtered?

Yes, in the toolbar (`smart-cal-toolbar`), **non-teacher** users get:

- **教室** `roomFilter` (select)
- **搜尋老師** `teacherSearch`
- **搜尋學生** `studentSearch` (narrows to teachers who have matching courses for the current day logic inside `visibleTeachers`)
- **`filterTeacherId`** (e.g. from `initialTeacherId` / external focus) — single-teacher filter inside `visibleTeachers`

See lines 64–72 and 66–72 in the first read.

**Week-overview “老師” chips** (`weekViewTeacherIds`) appear when `visibleTeachers.length > 1` and **`!isTeacher`** (lines 74–99). Those chips **filter courses in week overview** (`getCoursesForWeekCell`, etc.), **not** which columns appear in the **day** teacher grid (`v-for="teacher in visibleTeachers"` is unchanged by `weekViewTeacherIds`).

---

### 8. How `visibleTeachers` is computed — all teachers?

**No.** It starts from **`filterTeacherOptions`**: active profiles plus any teacher IDs/names found on **`courses`**. Then it applies **room**, **teacher search**, **student search** (via `filteredCourses` / `courseMatchesStudentSearch` and day scope), **`filterTeacherId`**, and **`isTeacher`** (only current teacher, with a fallback row if options are stale). Result is **sorted** by `roomLabel` then `username`.

```1575:1628:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const visibleTeachers = computed(() => {
  const teacherList = filterTeacherOptions.value.map(t => {
    ...
  });
  let filtered = teacherList;
  if (roomFilter.value) { ... }
  if (teacherSearch.value) { ... }
  if (studentSearch.value.trim()) { ... }
  if (filterTeacherId.value) { ... }
  if (isTeacher.value && currentTeacherId.value) { ... }
  return filtered.sort((a, b) => { ... });
});
```

---

### 9. `teacher-grid` / `teacher-col` CSS (width, min-width, flex)

```3525:3588:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.teacher-grid {
  display: grid;
  min-width: 0;
}
...
.teacher-col {
  border-right: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e2e8f0);
  min-width: 0;
}
...
.teacher-col-info { min-width: 0; flex: 1; }
.teacher-col-name {
  ...
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
```

Grid columns are sized by **`gridTemplateColumns`**; `.teacher-col` does **not** set an explicit width—only **`min-width: 0`** so grid items can shrink and ellipsis can work in the flex children.

---

### 10. Existing “compact” visual adjustments (`teacher-grid-compact`)

```3529:3560:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .teacher-col-header {
  height: 56px;
  padding: 6px 6px;
  gap: 5px;
}
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .col-header-blank {
  height: 56px;
}
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .teacher-col-avatar {
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
  font-size: 11px;
  border-radius: 6px;
}
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .teacher-col-name { font-size: 12px; }
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .teacher-col-room { font-size: 9px; }
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .course-block { ... }
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .cb-student { font-size: 11px; }
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .cb-detail,
.teacher-grid.teacher-grid-compact .cb-type { ... }
```

Additionally, when compact, the **capacity badge text is omitted** (only the colored badge remains; `title` still holds the tooltip):

```187:193:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
                >{{ isTeacherGridCompact ? '' : getSlotOccupancy(teacher.id, selectedDow, h).label }}</span>
```

---

### Summary: column width mechanism, what breaks with many teachers, what compact does

| Topic | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| **Column width mechanism** | CSS Grid: **56px** time column + **N equal `1fr` tracks** with `minmax(0, 1fr)`. No per-teacher minimum width on desktop. |
| **Many teachers (desktop)** | Columns become **very narrow**; names/rooms use **ellipsis**; course blocks get tight; **no** horizontal scroll (`overflow-x: hidden`). |
| **Compact mode (`≥10` teachers)** | Smaller header (64→56px), smaller avatar and fonts, tighter course blocks, **capacity label text hidden** in badges—**does not** add horizontal scroll on desktop; it only **reduces chrome** so slightly more fits when columns are already squeezed. |

**Toolbar area (lines 3155–3200):** That block is mostly **layout for the toolbar** (flex wrap, grid for filters + actions, `min-width: 0` / `max-width: 100%`). The actual filter controls are in the lines above (month/week/jump date + secondary row with filters and chips).

